@startuml
title COLORS - Use Case Diagram
left to right direction
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam usecaseBackgroundColor #EAF2F8
skinparam ArrowColor #34495E

actor "Existing user" as User
rectangle "COLORS web application" {
  usecase "Log in" as Login
  usecase "Add a color" as Add
  usecase "Search saved colors" as Search
  usecase "Log out" as Logout
}
User -- Login
User -- Add
User -- Search
User -- Logout

note right of Login
  Enter username and password.
  Matching credentials open color.html;
  invalid credentials display an error.
end note
note right of Add
  Precondition: user has logged in.
  Save a color name with the user's ID.
end note
note right of Search
  Precondition: user has logged in.
  Search names by partial text for that user.
  Empty text matches all of their colors.
end note
note right of Logout
  Clear browser login data and cookie;
  return to index.html.
end note
legend bottom
  Scope: existing accounts only; no registration, editing, or deletion.
  Login is a precondition for color use cases, not a repeated included use case.
  The PHP API trusts the supplied userId; login state is held in the browser.
endlegend
@enduml
